# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not housekeeping. `registry.rs` embeds the data files with
# `include_str!`, and two of its tests inject a fault by replacing a substring
# that spans a line break. When Git handed the working tree CRLF, those
# substrings stopped matching, the injection silently did nothing, and the tests
# went on asserting that *valid* data was rejected -- passing data through and
# failing for a reason unrelated to what they check.
*               text=auto eol=lf

*.rs            text eol=lf
*.ron           text eol=lf
*.wgsl          text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf

*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.lsw           binary
